Course outcomes
On completing the material you will be able to:

distinguish linear, non-linear and threshold concentration-response models, and say which is appropriate for a given endpoint;
identify the statistical distribution appropriate to a response variable, and fit a generalised model accordingly;
fit concentration-response models in R and plot the results;
derive NEC, NSEC and ECx estimates, and explain what each of them measures;
apply model averaging across a candidate set, and interpret the weights;
produce complete workflows for estimating no-effect toxicity suitable for use in species sensitivity distribution derivation.
